", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 53340, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_012pHwKKTmbD5eFgreEN7gzS", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 54524, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_019dBuKZknnv9jqXXRN77kJZ", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 54824, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_019dBuKZknnv9jqXXRN77kJZ", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 54824, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_019dBuKZknnv9jqXXRN77kJZ", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 60216, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n**Rollback**\n- **Before:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production.\n- **First try:** the first rollback stopped partway with an orchestrator error. Only us-east had moved to v2.3.0; us-west and eu-west were still on v2.3.1.\n- **Retry:** I ran the same rollback again and it finished. A status check shows all three regions on v2.3.0, the service healthy, and the error rate down to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to open the incident timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying and found it had been created, so I didn't submit it again. That avoided a duplicate incident and a second page to on-call.\n- **INC-0001 (SEV2, open):** it says v2.3.1 was failing, that it was rolled back to v2.3.0, that the first rollback attempt partly failed and the retry worked, and that the service is healthy now. It also asks for the v2.3.1 problem to be investigated before redeploying, since the v2.3.1 release candidate was also unhealthy.\n\nBecause v2.3.1 has never been healthy in production, redeploying it needs change-manager approval under org policy.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01CKjXAoqn35adB2iHXL3g98", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01FpiDS6UPGLEzB1254hSEpq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01DQWZ5DWY6Ya4LJ5qZm21vx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014kf1CrJRRnahMkSphPkg8Q", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Rollback was only partly applied: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same target again is safe, so I'll retry.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Cq5X6C6RActSWhEFRZsMSw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01PgeF9gx3WEszDyjaa11UU9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01N5vbq66PcZdE79fPJynot9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_012pHwKKTmbD5eFgreEN7gzS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of ~18%. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt partially failed (orchestrator error after us-east, leaving us-west/eu-west on v2.3.1); a retry completed successfully. Current state: all regions on v2.3.0, service healthy, error rate ~0.2%. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 regression (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy) before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_019dBuKZknnv9jqXXRN77kJZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n**Rollback**\n- **Before:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production.\n- **First try:** the first rollback stopped partway with an orchestrator error. Only us-east had moved to v2.3.0; us-west and eu-west were still on v2.3.1.\n- **Retry:** I ran the same rollback again and it finished. A status check shows all three regions on v2.3.0, the service healthy, and the error rate down to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to open the incident timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying and found it had been created, so I didn't submit it again. That avoided a duplicate incident and a second page to on-call.\n- **INC-0001 (SEV2, open):** it says v2.3.1 was failing, that it was rolled back to v2.3.0, that the first rollback attempt partly failed and the retry worked, and that the service is healthy now. It also asks for the v2.3.1 problem to be investigated before redeploying, since the v2.3.1 release candidate was also unhealthy.\n\nBecause v2.3.1 has never been healthy in production, redeploying it needs change-manager approval under org policy.", "type": "text"}]}]}